From: openEuler RISC-V packaging <packaging@openeuler.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] examples: do not dereference end() on the initial empty tree

The default test_hayne example calls find_nearest() before inserting its
first point. The empty-tree overload returns end(), which the iterator
contract explicitly forbids dereferencing. Check that sentinel before the
existing value comparison. Keep the full insertion/deletion loops and all
original assertions unchanged. This fixes the example caller, not the
library's search or erase semantics.

Not submitted upstream. Applies to official v0.7.5 commit
9b0cbb264393cbd40641256668393ef5bdbfe242.
Removal condition: a stable official release handles the empty initial tree.
--- a/examples/test_hayne.cpp
+++ b/examples/test_hayne.cpp
@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@

       //check if duplet with same coordinate already in vector/tree. If not: insert in vector and tree
       duplet_tree_type::iterator pItr = dupl_tree_test.find_nearest(super_dupre,std::numeric_limits<double>::max()).first;
-      if (*pItr!=super_dupre)
+      if (pItr == dupl_tree_test.end() || *pItr!=super_dupre)
       {
          dupl_tree_test.insert(super_dupre);
          vDuplets.push_back(super_dupre);
